---
source: crates/egress/src/lib.rs
expression: table
---
# unknown field
{"egress":"public","allowNone":true}
unknown field `allowNone`, expected one of `egress`, `allowAll`, `allowedNames`, `declaredCidrs`, `ttlFloorSecs`, `ttlCapSecs` at line 1 column 30

# unknown egress mode
{"egress":"partial"}
unknown variant `partial`, expected `none` or `public` at line 1 column 19

# egress absent
{"allowAll":true}
missing field `egress` at line 1 column 17

# malformed json
{"egress":"public",}
trailing comma at line 1 column 20

# allowAll under egress none
{"egress":"none","allowAll":true}
allowAll is set with egress "none", which allows nothing; set egress to "public" or clear allowAll

# allowedNames and declaredCidrs are dormant under egress none, not refused
{"egress":"none","allowedNames":["pypi.org"],"declaredCidrs":["93.184.216.0/24"]}
accepted: egress=None allowAll=false allowedNames=[Exact("pypi.org")] declaredCidrs=[93.184.216.0/24] ttl=90..3600

# ttlFloorSecs zero
{"egress":"public","ttlFloorSecs":0}
ttlFloorSecs is 0, which would hold a resolved address forever

# ttlFloorSecs above ttlCapSecs
{"egress":"public","ttlFloorSecs":7200,"ttlCapSecs":3600}
ttlFloorSecs 7200 is above ttlCapSecs 3600

# ttlCapSecs above the maximum
{"egress":"public","ttlCapSecs":604800}
ttlCapSecs 604800 is above the maximum 86400

# allowedNames non-ASCII
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["café.example"]}
allowedNames "café.example" is not ASCII; write the punycode (xn--) form, which is what a query carries

# allowedNames trailing dot
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["pypi.org."]}
allowedNames "pypi.org." has a trailing dot; write the name without it

# allowedNames single label
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["localhost"]}
allowedNames "localhost" is a single label, which cannot resolve publicly

# allowedNames all-numeric top label
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["169.254.169.254"]}
allowedNames "169.254.169.254" ends in an all-numeric label; allowedNames takes names, not addresses

# allowedNames empty label
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["files..acmeco.example"]}
allowedNames "files..acmeco.example" has an empty label

# allowedNames hyphen-bounded label
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["-files.acmeco.example"]}
allowedNames "-files.acmeco.example" has a label bounded by a hyphen: "-files"

# allowedNames underscore
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["build_cache.acmeco.example"]}
allowedNames "build_cache.acmeco.example" has a label outside [a-z0-9-]: "build_cache"

# allowedNames empty string
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":[""]}
allowedNames contains an empty name

# allowedNames lowercased and deduplicated
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["PyPI.ORG","pypi.org","artifacts.acmeco.example"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[Exact("pypi.org"), Exact("artifacts.acmeco.example")] declaredCidrs=[] ttl=90..3600

# allowedNames a name and its wildcard are distinct grants
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["acmeco.example","*.acmeco.example"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[Exact("acmeco.example"), Subdomains("acmeco.example")] declaredCidrs=[] ttl=90..3600

# allowedNames wildcard lowercased and deduplicated
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.ACMEco.example","*.acmeco.example"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[Subdomains("acmeco.example")] declaredCidrs=[] ttl=90..3600

# allowedNames wildcard alone
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*"]}
allowedNames "*" has a wildcard other than a leading "*.", the only form supported

# allowedNames wildcard with no base
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*."]}
allowedNames "*." has a trailing dot; write the name without it

# allowedNames two wildcard labels
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.*.acmeco.example"]}
allowedNames "*.*.acmeco.example" has a wildcard other than a leading "*.", the only form supported

# allowedNames doubled star
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["**.acmeco.example"]}
allowedNames "**.acmeco.example" has a wildcard other than a leading "*.", the only form supported

# allowedNames star without its dot
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*acmeco.example"]}
allowedNames "*acmeco.example" has a wildcard other than a leading "*.", the only form supported

# allowedNames star inside a label
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["api*.acmeco.example"]}
allowedNames "api*.acmeco.example" has a wildcard other than a leading "*.", the only form supported

# allowedNames wildcard label in the middle
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["api.*.acmeco.example"]}
allowedNames "api.*.acmeco.example" has a wildcard other than a leading "*.", the only form supported

# allowedNames wildcard label last
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["acmeco.*"]}
allowedNames "acmeco.*" has a wildcard other than a leading "*.", the only form supported

# allowedNames wildcard with a trailing dot
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.acmeco.example."]}
allowedNames "*.acmeco.example." has a trailing dot; write the name without it

# allowedNames wildcard over an invalid label
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.-acmeco.example"]}
allowedNames "*.-acmeco.example" has a label bounded by a hyphen: "-acmeco"

# allowedNames wildcard over a top-level domain
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.com"]}
allowedNames "*.com" is a wildcard over the public suffix "com", in the Public Suffix List's ICANN section; names beneath a public suffix belong to unrelated registrants

# allowedNames wildcard over an ICANN second-level suffix
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.co.uk"]}
allowedNames "*.co.uk" is a wildcard over the public suffix "co.uk", in the Public Suffix List's ICANN section; names beneath a public suffix belong to unrelated registrants

# allowedNames wildcard over a private suffix
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.github.io"]}
allowedNames "*.github.io" is a wildcard over the public suffix "github.io", in the Public Suffix List's private section; names beneath a public suffix belong to unrelated registrants

# allowedNames wildcard over a domain registered beneath a private suffix
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.acmeco.github.io"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[Subdomains("acmeco.github.io")] declaredCidrs=[] ttl=90..3600

# allowedNames wildcard over a domain holding private suffixes: only the base is checked
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.amazonaws.com"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[Subdomains("amazonaws.com")] declaredCidrs=[] ttl=90..3600

# allowedNames wildcard over a suffix made by a wildcard rule
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.acmeco.ck"]}
allowedNames "*.acmeco.ck" is a wildcard over the public suffix "acmeco.ck", in the Public Suffix List's ICANN section; names beneath a public suffix belong to unrelated registrants

# allowedNames wildcard over an exception to a wildcard rule
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.www.ck"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[Subdomains("www.ck")] declaredCidrs=[] ttl=90..3600

# allowedNames wildcard over a domain holding a wildcard rule: only the base is checked
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.kawasaki.jp"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[Subdomains("kawasaki.jp")] declaredCidrs=[] ttl=90..3600

# allowedNames wildcard over an exception beneath that wildcard rule
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.city.kawasaki.jp"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[Subdomains("city.kawasaki.jp")] declaredCidrs=[] ttl=90..3600

# allowedNames wildcard over an internationalized suffix, in punycode
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.xn--55qx5d.cn"]}
allowedNames "*.xn--55qx5d.cn" is a wildcard over the public suffix "xn--55qx5d.cn", in the Public Suffix List's ICANN section; names beneath a public suffix belong to unrelated registrants

# allowedNames wildcard over an unlisted top-level domain
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.example"]}
allowedNames "*.example" is a wildcard over the public suffix "example", by the Public Suffix List's default rule, which makes every top-level label a suffix; names beneath a public suffix belong to unrelated registrants

# allowedNames wildcard beneath an unlisted top-level domain
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["*.acmeco.example"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[Subdomains("acmeco.example")] declaredCidrs=[] ttl=90..3600

# allowedNames exact names are not checked against the list
{"egress":"public","allowedNames":["s3.amazonaws.com","github.io","co.uk"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[Exact("s3.amazonaws.com"), Exact("github.io"), Exact("co.uk")] declaredCidrs=[] ttl=90..3600

# declaredCidrs unparsable
{"egress":"public","declaredCidrs":["not-a-cidr"]}
declaredCidrs "not-a-cidr" has no prefix length; write an address and a prefix length, such as 10.0.0.0/8, or 10.0.0.1/32 for one address

# declaredCidrs with host bits set
{"egress":"public","declaredCidrs":["93.184.216.5/24"]}
declaredCidrs "93.184.216.5/24" sets bits below its prefix length; write 93.184.216.0/24, or 93.184.216.5/32 for one address

# declaredCidrs IPv6
{"egress":"public","declaredCidrs":["fd00::/8"]}
declaredCidrs "fd00::/8" is IPv6; only IPv4 ranges are supported

# declaredCidrs in the former shape, with ports
{"egress":"public","declaredCidrs":[{"cidr":"93.184.216.0/24","ports":[443]}]}
invalid type: map, expected a string at line 1 column 36

# declaredCidrs overlapping and repeated, kept disjoint
{"egress":"public","declaredCidrs":["93.184.216.128/25","93.184.216.0/24","93.184.216.0/24"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[] declaredCidrs=[93.184.216.0/24] ttl=90..3600

# declaredCidrs private (RFC1918)
{"egress":"public","declaredCidrs":["10.2.0.0/16"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[] declaredCidrs=[10.2.0.0/16] ttl=90..3600

# declaredCidrs cloud metadata and loopback
{"egress":"public","declaredCidrs":["169.254.169.254/32","127.0.0.1/32"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[] declaredCidrs=[127.0.0.1/32, 169.254.169.254/32] ttl=90..3600

# declaredCidrs every address
{"egress":"public","declaredCidrs":["10.89.0.0/24","0.0.0.0/0"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=false allowedNames=[] declaredCidrs=[0.0.0.0/0] ttl=90..3600

# declaredCidrs beside allowAll
{"egress":"public","allowAll":true,"declaredCidrs":["10.2.0.0/16"]}
accepted: egress=Public allowAll=true allowedNames=[] declaredCidrs=[10.2.0.0/16] ttl=90..3600
